  "description": "CR 717.2a: Innkeeper's Talent's level 2 ward and level 3 doubling are absent until it reaches each level. At the beginning of combat on alice's turn (CR 603.2) it puts a +1/+1 counter on target creature she controls; at level 2 her permanents with counters have ward {1} (CR 702.21a, 122.1); at level 3 counters she would put are doubled (CR 614.1a).",
  "note": "Turn 1 at level 1: bob's Shock on the countered Bears draws no ward trigger. Turn 3 at level 2: his Bolt on them does, and is countered when he declines to pay; his Shock on the counterless Hill Giant draws none, nor does alice's Shock on bob's countered Storm Crow; the turn-3 counter is still single, so level 3 is off. Turn 5 at level 3 the trigger's one counter becomes two.",
